    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0464" n="340" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg340"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3979: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Ruddock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-07-28T11:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 28,
                                1921—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 28—8:30
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>272. Canton reports Nanning and principal towns eastern Kwangsi captured. Li
                    Lu-ting [<hi rendition="#italic">Lu Yung-ting?</hi>]<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d290-f1"/> has fled. Recapture Pakhoi expected daily. Kwangsi
                    practically under control Kwangtung.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ruddock</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d290-f1" n="15" xml:id="d290-f1-content">
                <p>Inspector General of Kwangtung and Kwangsi.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
